<%# One kind: its icon, the number waiting on a maintainer, and — beside it, only
    when there is one — the number answered and held open.

    Held has no icon of its own. It used to, and the same open-hand appeared
    twice in a five-segment badge, once for bug reports and once for feature
    requests, which read as two unrelated things and left every number looking
    as though it belonged to the icon after it (owner, 2026-09-21). One icon per
    kind, and both of that kind's numbers beside it. %>
<span class="kind"><%= link_to path, title: tip, data: { tip: tip } do %><%= render "layouts/icon_#{icon}" %><%= n %><% end %><% if local_assigns[:held] && local_assigns[:held][:n].positive? %><span class="plus" aria-hidden="true">+</span><%= link_to local_assigns[:held][:n], local_assigns[:held][:path], class: "held", title: local_assigns[:held][:tip], data: { tip: local_assigns[:held][:tip] } %><% end %></span>
